 "result_text": "Fixed: the order of magic and non-magic patterns no longer changes the result of `glob`.\n\nThe cause was what the issue described. `curdir` was set once before the loop in `Glob.glob()` in `wcmatch/glob.py`, and a non-magic pattern like `dummy` overwrote it. The next magic pattern then globbed from `dummy` instead of the current directory. I moved the assignment inside the loop so each pattern starts from the current directory.\n\nI ran `glob(['**/glob.py', 'dummy'])` and the reversed list. Both now return `['wcmatch/glob.py']`. I didn't run the test suite or add a test.",
